  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, sorry you're having trouble. I'd like to help, but I need a bit more detail first. Could you tell me: 1) What isn't working (email, Teams, an app, VPN, signing in, something else)? 2) What happens when you try, including the exact wording of any error message? 3) When did it start, and does anyone near you have the same problem? A screenshot would help too. One thing I noticed while looking into this: your mailbox is almost completely full (about 99%). That can stop email from sending or syncing. If email is the problem, you can free up space right away. Empty your Deleted Items and Junk Email folders, sort your Inbox and Sent Items by size, then delete large attachments or save them to OneDrive. If you need to keep old mail, we can help you turn on Online Archive. Once I hear back, I'll pick this up again.",
  "internal_note": "The ticket was vague ('it's not working'), so I asked the user what's wrong. I looked up the user: Mei Chen (ID 9), Operations, account active, 0 failed sign-ins, not blocked, VPN enabled, password not expired. The mailbox is at 99.4% (50890 of 51200 MB), which likely explains it if this is an email problem (sending stops at 100%). I sent her the KB-010 cleanup steps. Laptop BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15) is online, checked in recently, has 14.6% disk free, and shows no warnings. I took no actions. Next step: wait for her details. If this is about email and she's still over 95% after cleanup, escalate per KB-010 for a quota increase (needs manager approval).",
